# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — AGENTS.md

## Purpose

This file is the single source of truth for AI collaboration rules in this repository. It carries only the minimal high-level rules and operating invariants every AI must always know. Details route into `aiDoc/` and are not expanded here.

## Loading Model

- **L0 standing rules**: this file and applicable directory-level rules. See the tool entry points below.
- **L1 task routing**: use `aiDoc/README.md` when locating code, confirming constraints, or recording a change.
- **L2 on-demand reading**: identify the affected path, component, or interface and open the relevant pages or sections. Look up record bodies for the current task as needed.
- **Conflict priority** (for in-repo tasks): `AGENTS.md` > `aiDoc/README.md` > aiDoc child docs > tool adapter files.

## Tool Loading

| Tool | Loading mechanism |
|---|---|
| Claude Code | Root `CLAUDE.md` natively imports `@AGENTS.md`; tool directories hold project commands only, never rule copies |
| Codex | Discovers `AGENTS.md` natively |
| Trae | Thin adapter points to `AGENTS.md` (entry pointer only) |
| Cursor / Copilot / other | If `@import` is unsupported, create a thin adapter from the template: entry pointers only, never copied rule bodies |

No tool-private directory may hold a copy of project-level rules.

